#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/math/index.rst:38
msgid ""
"The result uses round-to-nearest semantics. Vectorized loops may lower the "
"operation to packed FMA instructions when the target supports them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/math/index.rst:46
msgid ""
"For non-NaN operands, requires ``limit > 0`` and returns "
"``copysign(min(abs(x), limit), x)``, preserving the sign of zero. Supports "
"float16, bfloat16, and float32 with matching operand dtypes. Python numeric "
"limits are converted to the input's element dtype; a scalar limit is "
"broadcast to vector inputs. The caller supplies a positive limit for "
"clipping semantics. No runtime check is emitted: scalar inputs lower to one "
"PTX instruction. Even-width float16/bfloat16 vectors use packed x2 "
"instructions, one per pair. Float32 vectors use one instruction per lane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/cuda/language/math/index.rst:56
msgid ""
"If either operand is NaN, the result is a canonical NaN; its original sign "
"and payload are not preserved. Nonpositive numeric limits are outside this "
"API's contract. Subnormals are preserved. Each operand is evaluated once."
msgstr ""
